     1,
     "<div lang=\"FR-CA\" link=\"blue\" vlink=\"purple\"><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-CA\">Hello.  I was surprised to read, in Beaujean’s book « Latent variable modeling using R », that there is a special operator for specifying formative latents : « &lt;~ ».  This doesn’t appear in any other documentation that I have found for lavaan and the book simply mentions it without going into any detail about it.  Can someone confirm that this operator actually exists in the current version of lavaan?  If so, can someone point me to documentation that gives more information about it?<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-CA\">Thanks.<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-CA\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-CA\">Bill Shipley<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-CA\">Laboratoire d’Écologie Fonctionnelle<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-CA\">Département de biologie, Université de Sherbrooke, Sherbrooke (Qc) Canada </span><span>J1K 2R1<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span><a href=\"tel:(819)%20821-8000\" value=\"+18198218000\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\">(819) 821-8000</a>, poste 62079<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span>Fax: <a href=\"tel:(819)%20821-8049\" value=\"+18198218049\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\">(819) 821-8049</a><u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-CA\"><a href=\"http://www.billshipley.recherche.usherbrooke.ca/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.billshipley.recherche.usherbrooke.ca/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792430172594000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1jdPOTiL5_nPqopIBtHm5Q\"><span lang=\"FR-CA\">http://www.billshipley.recherche.usherbrooke.ca/</span></a></span><span><u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
