    [
     1,
     "<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word\">It does. I have a few examples at <a href=\"http://byrneslab.net/classes/sem_notes/10_Composite_Variables.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://byrneslab.net/classes/sem_notes/10_Composite_Variables.pdf&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792430172597000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2MA1TkGdtnA31atNRIEH6e\">http://byrneslab.net/classes/sem_notes/10_Composite_Variables.pdf</a><div><br></div><div>It came about as I had some exchanges with Yves about the hack-y nature of how to implement composite variables (see the old way here: <a href=\"http://www.imachordata.com/ecological-sems-and-composite-variables-what-why-and-how/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.imachordata.com/ecological-sems-and-composite-variables-what-why-and-how/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792430172597000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0er43BzbqMOy9r-s3N886h\">http://www.imachordata.com/ecological-sems-and-composite-variables-what-why-and-how/</a> - which should still work).</div><div><br></div><div><br><div><blockquote type=\"cite\"></blockquote></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word\"><div><div><blockquote type=\"cite\"><div>On Mar 20, 2015, at 10:40 AM, Bill Shipley &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">bill.s...@usherbrooke.ca</a>&gt; wrote:</div><br></blockquote></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word\"><div><div><blockquote type=\"cite\"><div><div style=\"font-family:Helvetica;font-size:12px;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px\"><div style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span lang=\"EN-CA\">Hello.  I was surprised to read, in Beaujean’s book « Latent variable modeling using R », that there is a special operator for specifying formative latents : « &lt;~ ».  This doesn’t appear in any other documentation that I have found for lavaan and the book simply mentions it without going into any detail about it.  Can someone confirm that this operator actually exists in the current version of lavaan?  If so, can someone point me to documentation that gives more information about it?<u></u><u></u></span></div><div style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span lang=\"EN-CA\">Thanks.<u></u><u></u></span></div><div style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span lang=\"EN-CA\"> </span></div><div style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span lang=\"EN-CA\">Bill Shipley<u></u><u></u></span></div><div style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span lang=\"EN-CA\">Laboratoire d’Écologie Fonctionnelle<u></u><u></u></span></div><div style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span lang=\"EN-CA\">Département de biologie, Université de Sherbrooke, Sherbrooke (Qc) Canada<span> </span></span><span>J1K 2R1<u></u><u></u></span></div><div style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span><a href=\"tel:(819)%20821-8000\" value=\"+18198218000\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\">(819) 821-8000</a>, poste 62079<u></u><u></u></span></div><div style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span>Fax: <a href=\"tel:(819)%20821-8049\" value=\"+18198218049\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\">(819) 821-8049</a><u></u><u></u></span></div><div style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span lang=\"EN-CA\"><a href=\"http://www.billshipley.recherche.usherbrooke.ca/\" style=\"color:purple;text-decoration:underline\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.billshipley.recherche.usherbrooke.ca/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792430172597000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3dljWW09fNkEhEj_43_IaZ\"><span lang=\"FR-CA\">http://www.billshipley.recherche.usherbrooke.ca/</span></a></span><span><u></u><u></u></span></div><div style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><u></u> <u></u></div></div><div style=\"font-family:Helvetica;font-size:12px;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px\"><br></div></div></blockquote></div></div></div>"
