   "subject": "Re: operator for formative latents",
   "parts": [
    [
     2,
     "On 03/20/2015 03:40 PM, Bill Shipley wrote:\r<br>&gt; Hello.  I was surprised to read, in Beaujean’s book « Latent variable\r<br>&gt; modeling using R », that there is a special operator for specifying\r<br>&gt; formative latents : « &lt;~ ».  This doesn’t appear in any other\r<br>&gt; documentation that I have found for lavaan\r<br>\r<br>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "True. The lavaan documentation needs a serious update.\r<br>\r<br>The &quot;&lt;~&quot; operator is just syntax candy. It creates a latent variable \r<br>(with no indicators), and sets the (possibly residual) variance of this \r<br>latent variable to zero.\r<br>\r<br>So this syntax:\r<br>\r<br>f &lt;~ 1*x1 + x2 + x3\r<br>\r<br>is equivalent to\r<br>\r<br>f =~ 0\r<br>f ~~ 0*f\r<br>f ~ 1*x1 + x2 + x3\r<br>\r<br>Yves.\r<br>\r<br>"
    ]
   ]
  }
 ]
